{
  "schema_version": "report-evidence/1",
  "source_sha256": "5545daf7fcc6e2c1b49643199d6a627836345da2e7a0479cfe6d4107954824bd",
  "fragments": [
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0001",
      "text": "Hardcoded Zero Slippage in wiTryVaultComposer Causes DoS Due to LayerZero Dust Removal",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 86,
      "line": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0002",
      "text": "Summary",
      "start": 88,
      "end": 95,
      "line": 3
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0003",
      "text": "I found that wiTryVaultComposer sets minAmountLD equal to assets (amount sent) in both _fastRedeem() and _handleUnstake() functions. This configuration fails to account for LayerZero's mandatory dust removal mechanism, which truncates amounts to fit cross-chain decimal precision.",
      "start": 97,
      "end": 377,
      "line": 5
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0004",
      "text": "Since iTryTokenOFT inherits the default sharedDecimals of 6, any transfer amount not perfectly divisible by 10^12 will fail with SlippageExceeded. This results in a Denial of Service (DoS) for users attempting to redeem or unstake uneven amounts (which is extremely common due to yield accrual).",
      "start": 379,
      "end": 674,
      "line": 7
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0005",
      "text": "This exact issue was previously identified and fixed in LayerZero's OVault audit by Cantina, where it was rated as Medium severity.",
      "start": 676,
      "end": 807,
      "line": 9
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0006",
      "text": "Vulnerability Details",
      "start": 809,
      "end": 830,
      "line": 11
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0007",
      "text": "Looking at wiTryVaultComposer.sol, slippage is hardcoded to zero in two critical functions:",
      "start": 831,
      "end": 922,
      "line": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0008",
      "text": "1. _fastRedeem (Lines 116-117)",
      "start": 924,
      "end": 954,
      "line": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0009",
      "text": "Solidity",
      "start": 956,
      "end": 964,
      "line": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0010",
      "text": "_sendParam.amountLD = assets;",
      "start": 966,
      "end": 995,
      "line": 18
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0011",
      "text": "_sendParam.minAmountLD = assets; // <--- Vulnerability: 0% slippage",
      "start": 996,
      "end": 1063,
      "line": 19
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0012",
      "text": "2. _handleUnstake (Lines 267-268)",
      "start": 1064,
      "end": 1097,
      "line": 20
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0013",
      "text": "Solidity",
      "start": 1099,
      "end": 1107,
      "line": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0014",
      "text": "amountLD: assets,",
      "start": 1109,
      "end": 1126,
      "line": 24
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0015",
      "text": "minAmountLD: assets, // <--- Vulnerability: 0% slippage",
      "start": 1127,
      "end": 1182,
      "line": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0016",
      "text": "The Root Cause: LayerZero Dust Removal",
      "start": 1183,
      "end": 1221,
      "line": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0017",
      "text": "The LayerZero OFT standard forces dust removal before checking slippage. According to OFTCore.sol:",
      "start": 1222,
      "end": 1320,
      "line": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0018",
      "text": "Solidity",
      "start": 1322,
      "end": 1330,
      "line": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0019",
      "text": "function _debitView(uint256 _amountLD, uint256 _minAmountLD, uint32)",
      "start": 1332,
      "end": 1400,
      "line": 31
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0020",
      "text": "internal view virtual returns (uint256 amountSentLD, uint256 amountReceivedLD)",
      "start": 1406,
      "end": 1484,
      "line": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0021",
      "text": "{",
      "start": 1486,
      "end": 1487,
      "line": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0022",
      "text": "// @dev Remove the dust so nothing is lost on the conversion between chains",
      "start": 1492,
      "end": 1567,
      "line": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0023",
      "text": "amountSentLD = _removeDust(_amountLD);",
      "start": 1572,
      "end": 1610,
      "line": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0024",
      "text": "amountReceivedLD = amountSentLD;",
      "start": 1615,
      "end": 1647,
      "line": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0025",
      "text": "// @dev Check for slippage.",
      "start": 1653,
      "end": 1680,
      "line": 38
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0026",
      "text": "if (amountReceivedLD < _minAmountLD) {",
      "start": 1685,
      "end": 1723,
      "line": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0027",
      "text": "revert SlippageExceeded(amountReceivedLD, _minAmountLD); // <--- Reverts here",
      "start": 1732,
      "end": 1809,
      "line": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0028",
      "text": "}",
      "start": 1814,
      "end": 1815,
      "line": 41
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0029",
      "text": "}",
      "start": 1816,
      "end": 1817,
      "line": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0030",
      "text": "Since iTryTokenOFT.sol uses the default shared decimals of 6 and local decimals of 18, the conversion rate is 10^12.",
      "start": 1818,
      "end": 1934,
      "line": 43
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0031",
      "text": "Example: A user redeems 100.000000000000000001 tokens (1 wei of dust from yield).",
      "start": 1936,
      "end": 2017,
      "line": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0032",
      "text": "Dust Removal: 100.0...01 becomes 100.0...00.",
      "start": 2019,
      "end": 2063,
      "line": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0033",
      "text": "Check: 100.0...00 (received) < 100.0...01 (minAmount).",
      "start": 2065,
      "end": 2119,
      "line": 49
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0034",
      "text": "Result: Transaction Reverts.",
      "start": 2121,
      "end": 2149,
      "line": 51
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0035",
      "text": "Impact",
      "start": 2151,
      "end": 2157,
      "line": 53
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0036",
      "text": "Denial of Service: Users cannot use Fast Redeem or Unstake features if their balance includes any dust (which is almost guaranteed due to yield calculations).",
      "start": 2159,
      "end": 2317,
      "line": 55
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0037",
      "text": "Wasted Assets: Users pay for source chain execution and LayerZero messaging fees, only for the transaction to revert on the destination chain.",
      "start": 2319,
      "end": 2461,
      "line": 57
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0038",
      "text": "No Workaround: Since the slippage is hardcoded in the contract, users cannot manually adjust it to make their transactions succeed.",
      "start": 2463,
      "end": 2594,
      "line": 59
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0039",
      "text": "Prior Art",
      "start": 2596,
      "end": 2605,
      "line": 61
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0040",
      "text": "This is a known integration issue with LayerZero V2. Cantina identified this exact bug in LayerZero's own OVault implementation:",
      "start": 2607,
      "end": 2735,
      "line": 63
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0041",
      "text": "\"Different slippage checks can lead to stuck funds - executeOVaultAction() has a minAmount check, but LayerZeroEndpoint::send() has a slightly different minAmount check in _debitView(). With specific amounts, it could pass the first check but fail the second.\"",
      "start": 2737,
      "end": 2997,
      "line": 65
    },
    {
      "id": "e_5545daf7fcc6_0042",
      "text": "Source: Cantina Audit - LayerZero OVault",
      "start": 2999,
      "end": 3039,
      "line": 67
    }
  ]
}
